        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "Toronto's offseason has detonated with a blockbuster that redefines the franchise's entire identity, proving GM John Chayka isn't playing it safe. <strong>Sergei Bobrovsky agrees to a three-year, $21M deal with the Maple Leafs</strong>, injecting two-time Stanley Cup pedigree into a crease that faltered after missing the playoffs last season with 78 points and an 8th-place Atlantic standing. The 37-year-old goalie, who posted a 27-23-1 record last year, arrives as the immediate story, while Chayka's roster overhaul - trading Joseph Woll and Nick Robertson to clear cap space - signals a bold reset. This isn't just a goalie swap; it's a statement that the Leafs are desperate to turn the tide. <strong>What to watch now: how Bobrovsky's presence reshapes the team's defensive confidence heading into next season</strong>.",
