      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "With a packed Rogers Centre and the nation watching on Canada Day, the Blue Jays finally delivered a stress-free afternoon of baseball against a stubborn Mets squad. <strong>Sean Keys' first Major League home run sparked a 9-3 rout</strong>, silencing critics and giving the 41-46 team, sitting 11 games back in the AL East, a genuine flicker of Wild Card hope. Keys, joined by Spencer Miles' three scoreless innings, embodied the surge needed to break their recent slump, while Guerrero Jr. showed subtle signs of progress after a tough stretch. The series win over New York offers a rare momentum boost, but the road remains steep with 11 games to catch the division leader. <strong>Next up, Saturday's 10:10 PM ET trip to Seattle against the Mariners</strong>, where the Jays must prove this Canada Day win was just the start of a serious run.",
        "updated": "Updated July 2, 2026"
